[ext_resource type="Script" path="res://game/scenes/BattleCameraRig.cs" id="3_rig"]

; ============================================================================================
; The battle, drawn as a stage the fight is fought on.
;
; 🔴 Every distance, timing and camera number on this screen's exports is a CHOICE OF THIS TASK
; and not one of them is authored by a design document. The design states how a fight must READ —
; the hero on the left facing the enemies on the right, a swing that reaches, a blow that
; recoils, a fall that stays down, plates over heads, the whole stage in the band the interface
; leaves free — and states no distance, no duration and no angle at all. Per steering rule S6
; they live here, in one greppable place, marked as debt owed to a ruling, rather than as
; constants scattered through the code where they would read as decided.
;
; What IS authored is derived rather than picked: the camera's distance solves itself from the
; stage's real extent at the viewport's real aspect, and its lift from the band the interface
; leaves free (BattleCameraRig.UsableBandTop/Bottom). The enemy heights come off the shipped
; models, not off a number here.
;
; ⚠️ The two facing yaws are the one place the art's own convention shows: every model ships
; facing +Z, the way glTF faces, and an actor rig looks along its own -Z, so both the hero and the
; enemy template are turned 180 to look across the stage.
;
; ⚠️ There is no WorldEnvironment and no light here, and there must not be: a viewport has exactly
; one environment, and AppRoot owns it along with the app-wide key and fill. The floor is a real
; plane that takes the key light's shadow, not a quad pinned in front of the camera — a rig that
; frames the stage would leave a pinned quad behind.
;
; ⚠️ Nothing here reflects anything: the floor's material leaves the engine's default surface
; alone, because a reflective one renders black under a build with no probe and no sky.
;
; ⚠️ Every type size, colour and gap on the overlay is a per-node override owed to the UI kit,
; chosen against the engine's default font, and has to be re-checked when the real faces land.
; ============================================================================================

